<div class="docs-hero">
  <h1>Get started</h1>
  <p>Flint UI is two files — <code>flint.css</code> (~800 lines) and
     <code>flint.js</code> (~50 lines). No build step, no dependencies, no
     webfonts. Copy them in and use the classes.</p>
</div>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="gs-quickstart">Quick start</h2>
  <p>Grab the two files from the repo and link them — the script is deferred
     and tiny, so order doesn't matter:</p>
  {% from "macros.njk" import snippet with context %}
  {% set quickStart %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="css/flint.css">
<script src="js/flint.js" defer></script>
{% endset %}
  {{ snippet(quickStart) }}
  <p>Then pick a shell and paste its markup — every component page's
     <strong>Implementation</strong> tab has a copy-paste-ready starting point,
     and <code>demos/*.html</code> in the repo are full working pages.</p>
</section>

