<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="gs-selection">Selection: <code>aria-current="page"</code></h2>
  <p>One attribute drives every selected state — nav rows, tabs, list rows all
     key off <code>aria-current="page"</code>. With <code>flint.js</code>
     loaded, clicking inside any <code>data-fl-nav</code> container moves it
     automatically (anchors still navigate). Without JS, set it yourself —
     which is what you want with server routing anyway:</p>
  {% set selection %}
<nav class="fl-tab-bar" data-fl-nav aria-label="Primary">
  <button class="fl-tab" aria-current="page">…</button>  <!-- selected -->
  <button class="fl-tab">…</button>
</nav>
{% endset %}
  {{ snippet(selection) }}
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="gs-nojs">Works without JS</h2>
  <p>Everything renders correctly with JavaScript disabled. <code>flint.js</code>
     only adds two conveniences:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Selected-state reflection</strong> on click (with server routing
        you set <code>aria-current</code> yourself).</li>
    <li><strong>Drawer toggling</strong> — the open/close buttons and scrim work
        through it. Without JS, control the drawer by toggling
        <code>fl-drawer-open</code> on <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> yourself, or
        call <code>flint.drawer(true/false)</code>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Icons are empty placeholder squares (a <code>fl-icon</code> span renders a
     gray block) — swap in any real icon set without touching other markup;
     sizes are fixed by the surrounding component classes.</p>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="gs-tokens">Tokens</h2>
  <p>The whole look is ~30 CSS custom properties on <code>:root</code> in
     <code>flint.css</code>. The essentials:</p>
  <table class="docs-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Token</th><th>Default</th><th>Role</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-accent</code></td><td><code>#1a73e8</code></td><td>Selection, links, focus, filled buttons</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-tint</code></td><td><code>#e8f0fe</code></td><td>Selected-state fills (pills, rows)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-border</code></td><td><code>#dadce0</code></td><td>Every border — replaces every shadow</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-font</code></td><td><code>system-ui</code></td><td>OS default — no webfont; override to brand</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-radius</code> / <code>--fl-radius-card</code></td><td><code>4px</code> / <code>8px</code></td><td>Corner radii</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-topbar-h</code></td><td><code>64px</code> (56px &lt;600px)</td><td>Top bar height</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-content-max</code></td><td><code>960px</code></td><td>Desktop reading column</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-dur</code> / <code>--fl-ease</code></td><td><code>150ms</code></td><td>Motion</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Override inline or in your own stylesheet — no rebuild:</p>
  {% set theme %}
:root {
  --fl-accent: #188038;    /* green Google */
  --fl-tint: #e6f4ea;
}
{% endset %}
  {{ snippet(theme) }}
  <p>Each component page's <strong>Theming</strong> section lists the tokens it
     actually consumes.</p>
</section>

